# =============================================================================
# EC2DEMO — local Vite dev pointed at the live EC2 backend (Spring profile: ec2demo)
# =============================================================================
# Activated by: `npm run dev:ec2demo`  (mode = ec2demo)
#
# Pairs with `application-ec2demo.properties` on the EC2 instance. Use this
# when you want to iterate on frontend code against real backend state — live
# projects, real FL-server lifecycle, real WebSocket logs.
#
# How it works:
#   - Browser hits http://localhost:5173/api/* and ws://localhost:5173/ws-logs
#   - Vite proxies BOTH to https://fedlearn.duckdns.org (see vite.config.ts).
#   - Cookies are first-party to localhost:5173 — sidesteps cross-origin /
#     third-party-cookie issues that would otherwise break Safari.
#
# To point at a different EC2 host (e.g. a teammate's deployment), override
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET in .env.local or .env.ec2demo.local — both gitignored.
# =============================================================================

VITE_FEDLEARN_API_URL=http://localhost:5173/api
VITE_SERVER_ROOT_URL=http://localhost:5173
VITE_PROXY_TARGET=https://fedlearn.duckdns.org
